From 3276feb0bc5406fe16292328f55234fdff080002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:30:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VAX8200: KLESI-B VAXBI tape adapter (device TB) and SET UBA
 DISABLE

KLESI-B (BI type 0103, ULTRIX V2.0 bla.c): a VAXBI node with the DWBUA's
registers and map in front of a TMSCP port at 774500 on its internal
Unibus.  New device TB (node 8, disabled by default, TU81 drives); VMS
V4.7 shows it as "BI - LESI Adapter" with the port PTB (MUB) next to the
TQ, or PTA (MUA) without the DWBUA.

- PDP11/pdp11_tq.c: the per-controller state is a context (TQ_CTX); the
  code serves several TMSCP controllers: TQ (controller 0, unchanged) and,
  on the VAX 8200, TB (controller 1).  Memory access and interrupts go
  through hooks of the context.
- VAX/vax820_klesib.c (new): the adapter (BIIC and DWBUA registers, map,
  window with the port, interrupts: vector offset | port vector).
- VAX/vax820_uba.c: the buffer routines take the adapter's map function
  (shared by DWBUA and KLESI-B); ReadIO/WriteIO pass the KLESI-B window on;
  SET UBA DISABLE (VAXBI-only mode) removes the DWBUA and disables every
  enabled Unibus device (refused while one is attached), SET UBA ENABLE
  restores them.
- VAX/vax820_defs.h: ADDR_IS_IO covers the DWBUA window only while the
  UBA is enabled, plus the KLESI-B window.
- makefile, VAX/CMakeLists.txt, VAX/vax820_syslist.c: the new file and
  device.

Tested with VMS V4.7: TU81 on the KLESI-B with and without the DWBUA, on
the 8200 and the 8300 (BACKUP, BACKUP/LIST, restore, DIFFERENCES); TK50
on TQ (MicroVAX II, VAX-11/750, realism mode); TU81 on TQ and the UDA50
boot on the DWBUA (8200).

Patch 11 v2: in the sound realism mode the KLESI-B connects TU81 drives
only (SET SOUND ENABLED, SET TB <type> and ATTACH refuse a TK50, TK70 or
TKUSER); no KLESI adapter ever had one.  The normal mode keeps SIMH's
choice of types.

Patch 11 v3: SET TB ENABLE in the realism mode makes a TB of another type
(chosen while TB was disabled) a TU81 and says so (known issues 77).

